    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before becoming a town, the area was a vast prairie that stretched near St. Louis, offering fertile ground for early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dardenne_Prairie%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dardenne Prairie began as Dardenne Township in 1821, became an incorporated town in 1981, and achieved city status in 2001.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Dardenne_Prairie,_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "French colonial explorers and fur traders first mapped the region in the mid‑1700s, setting the stage for later European settlement.",
